  "body": "## What changed\n\n`add_operation` and `edit_operation` (and the commands behind them, `CreateOperation`, `EditOperationParams` and `ChangeOperationKind`) refused a bad number with a sentence that does not name the field:\n\n> operation parameters are not usable for a 2D Pocket operation\n\nAn agent or a script user could not tell what to correct. Found in the local-model MCP benchmark of 2026-11-22.\n\nWhen `OpParams::is_sane` fails, a new helper, `commands/operation/field_refusal.rs`, reads the parameters through `project::params_to_json` (the field names that MCP and the project file use) and adds the first shared field that breaks its rule:\n\n- `stepdown`, `stepover`, `feed`, `plunge_feed`, `tolerance`, `helix_radius`: greater than 0\n- `stock_to_leave`: 0 or more\n\nNow:\n\n> operation parameters are not usable for a 2D Pocket operation: stepdown must be greater than 0 (got -3)\n\nNotes for the review:\n\n- Only top-level fields are read. Every kind that has one of these fields at the top level asks the same rule of it (checked against each arm of `is_sane` and the plasma, waterjet, wire, sinker and undercut doors). A nested block with its own rules, such as the wire's 4-axis `tolerance` (0..=10), is not read.\n- The helper runs only after `is_sane` has failed, so it can only name a field that really breaks its rule. If the cause is something else (a height, an angle, a kind-specific field), the refusal is the old sentence, unchanged.\n- The start of the sentence does not change, so tests and agents that match on \"operation parameters are not usable\" still match.\n- The project load check (`project/validate.rs`) is not changed.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New test `mcp_pockets::a_bad_pocket_parameter_is_refused_by_field_name`: `stepdown: -3` and `stock_to_leave: -0.5` through `edit_operation` (the operation is unchanged after the refusal), and `feed: 0` through `add_operation` (no operation is created).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base main`: 24 of 27 steps pass on the first run. The 3 red steps (`lib` `lathe_voice::tests::the_door_refuses_on_every_turning_dialect_and_passes_every_milling_one`, `sinker_burn`, `wire_tool`) failed with \"cannot find the file\" for the Sodick post and machine files: my `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` was inside another, older checkout, and the data folders resolve by walking up from the test exe. All three pass with a target dir outside any checkout.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --lib --test mcp_pockets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- By hand over MCP (`camcraft-cli mcp`), the same `edit_operation` call on `main` and on this branch gives the two sentences above.\n\nChangelog: An operation refused for a bad number now names the field and its rule, for example \"stepdown must be greater than 0 (got -3)\".\nEffort: low\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3545\n",
